hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2912","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, narrated to us Muhammad—meaning ibn Ja‘far—and Yahya ibn Sa‘id, Abu Dawud, ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, and Ibn Abi ‘Adiy, and Abu al-Walid, they all said: Narrated to us Shu‘bah, who said: I heard Sulayman ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman say: I heard ‘Ubayd ibn Fayruz say: I said to al-Bara’: “Tell me what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) disliked or forbade regarding sacrificial animals (al-adahi).”\nHe said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, gesturing with his hand while my hand is shorter than the Messenger of Allah’s (ﷺ) hand:\n“Four [types of animals] are not valid for sacrifice:\n1. The one with a clear defect in its eye (al-‘awra’ al-bayyin ‘awaruha),\n2. The one with a clear disease (al-mariḍah al-bayyin marḍuha),\n3. The lame one with a clear limp (al-‘arjā’ al-bayyin ṭala‘uha),\n4. And the emaciated one that has no marrow (al-kasīr allatī lā tanqa’).”\nHe [‘Ubayd] said: I also dislike a defect in the ear or the horn.\nHe [al-Bara’] said: Whatever you dislike, leave it, but do not forbid it for others.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
